# Line endings — S1a.9.3 T1a.9.3.3.
#
# The gate compares **bytes**: 37 `.expected` files, the DOT and trace goldens,
# `corpus_shapes.md5`, and `stdlib/MANIFEST.sha256`, which is a SHA-256 over
# every `std.*` module's contents. A checkout that rewrote LF to CRLF would
# change every one of those digests, and the failure would be a Windows-only
# wall of red that says nothing about Windows.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true`, so this is the difference
# between the corpus sweep meaning something on a Windows runner and it being
# a checkout artefact. Nothing in this repository is CRLF-sensitive in the
# other direction: there is no `.bat`, no `.ps1`, and no file git detects as
# binary.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named rather than left to detection, because these are the ones a byte
# comparison reads and a mis-detection would be silent.
*.ein       text eol=lf
*.expected  text eol=lf
*.dot       text eol=lf
*.md5       text eol=lf
*.sha256    text eol=lf
*.jsonl     text eol=lf
